# Commands run by the launchd job com.redwood.demo (RC_JOBS=rc.jobs.metaldrawall).
#
# Every fragment shader of AppleMetalGLRenderer's library, drawn through the Metal driver,
# one line each. One shader drawn is an example; air_run has drawn all of them on softpipe and
# compared the pixel (255 of 274 agreed with LLVM and were drawn, docs/air.md), so drawing them
# all here turns the example into coverage -- and tools/air/metalcheck.py produces each
# reference itself rather than trusting a number written into the test.
#
# One process for the whole library on purpose: the loader keeps the first 256 KB and the last
# 1 MB of a boot's log and drops the middle, so 271 processes would lose the middle of their own
# table.
/redwood/bin/metal_drv_test --draw-all /System/Library/Extensions/AppleMetalGLRenderer.bundle/default.metallib
